  "definition": "epoch 0 = the schedule T0 coincides with the first held FNAF2_NIGHT frame on the helper image clock; positive epoch fires the schedule later; the executor delivers T0 = onset + aimMs + k*periodMs, k in 0..1. The period is Withered Foxy's five-second roll timer (g337). The model carries g778 (a held hall light meets Golden Freddy in the office) as of 2026-09-13.",
  "why": "The first Night 6 binding (fnv1a-bc5e044c, mask off 9460, flash 10060, anchored at 3850) was refuted twice on the phone by Golden Freddy the second after a camdrop (docs/evidence/night6-anchored-golden-freddy-20260913.md): at that phase a five-second tick lands with the cameras up, where g336 creates him, and the camdrop's held light triggers g778 at the drop. With the mask off at 8960 and the flash at 9560, the winning band moves to effective epochs 5033-5417: the ticks land at cycle phases ~4.7 and ~9.7 -- after the drop and before the raise, so he is never created -- and the flash precedes the second tick, so D is fresh at both. Holes at 5117-5150 and 5317-5350 are the split-arming sampler (g263). Aim 0 on the 5000 ms grid: k=0 is the onset itself and is never authorized in time; k=1 delivers T0 = onset + 5000, effective [5200, 5285] inside the window [5166.67, 5316.67) with 33 ms to each hole. Both k rows are clean at 3000 seeds. REVISED after night6-anchoredb1 (aim 0, k=1, effective 5253): released 1.2 ms late, 32 gates agreed, died at 320 s (4 AM) to Withered Foxy at the instant of the post-mask flash (g573), no Golden Freddy. That is the band's upper (Foxy) edge, which the phone reaches ~100 ms sooner than the model because the mask-off takes 307 ms there against the model's 244 and the flash lands later. The aim moves to 4917 (k=0): effective [5117, 5202], the low half of the band.",
